---
import { links } from '../data/links';
---

<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="faq-title">Questions.</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="faq" data-reveal>
      <details>
        <summary><span>Why read-only?</span></summary>
        <div>
          <p>
            Listing servers and writing an ssh config only need read access, so that is all Rackbar asks for. A
            Read token cannot change anything in your project, whatever the app does with it. A menu bar is also
            one stray click from anything it offers, and nobody should restart a database by mistake.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary><span>Where are my tokens stored?</span></summary>
        <div>
          <p>
            In the data protection Keychain on your Mac: readable after first unlock, never synced. Not in
            UserDefaults, not on a command line. Rackbar tries a token before it keeps it, and removing a project
            deletes its tokens from the Keychain.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary><span>Does it work with several projects?</span></summary>
        <div>
          <p>
            That is what it is for. Add one token per Hetzner project, each under a label. Tokens that share a label
            share one heading and one ssh namespace, which helps when a customer's servers are spread over several
            projects. A refresh costs three requests per token, made side by side.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary><span>Why at the end of <code>~/.ssh/config</code>?</span></summary>
        <div>
          <p>Because ssh takes the first value it finds. Whatever you set above the <code>Include</code> wins over the generated entries:</p>
          <pre class="snippet"><span class="k">Host</span> acme/*
    <span class="k">User</span> deploy
    <span class="k">IdentityFile</span> ~/.ssh/work_ed25519

<span class="k">Host</span> acme/db-1
    <span class="k">ProxyJump</span> acme/bastion

<span class="k">Match</span> all
<span class="k">Include</span> hcloud/config</pre>
          <p><code>Match all</code> closes whatever <code>Host</code> block came last. Without it, the <code>Include</code> would only apply inside that block.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary><span>Is there a Linux version?</span></summary>
        <div>
          <p>
            Rackbar is macOS only. On Linux with Omarchy, its sibling
            <a href={links.omarchy}>omarchy-hcloud</a> does the same in the Omarchy bar.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
